==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|is|bʰeydʰ}}
From {{inh|is|non|bíða}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*bīdaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈpiːða/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|iːða|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|beið|biðu|beðið}}

# {{lb|is|intransitive}} to [[wait]]
#: '''''Bíddu''' eftir mér!''
#:: '''Wait''' for me!
#: '''''Bíddu'''!''
#:: '''Wait'''!
# {{lb|is|transitive|with genitive}} to [[wait for]] something{{jump|is|wait for|s}}
#: '''''Bíddu''' mín.''
#:: '''Wait for''' me.
# {{lb|is|transitive|with accusative}} to [[abide]], [[undergo]], [[suffer]] (some fate, usually something bad)
#: ''Karþagómenn '''biðu''' ósigur fyrir Rómverjum.''
#:: The Carthaginians '''suffered''' defeat at the hands of the Romans.

